      "SourceSection": "10.2: Going Around and Around and Around",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The center of a windmill is \\((0,0)\\) and it has 5 blades, each 1 meter in length. A point \\(P\\) is at the end of the blade that is pointing directly to the right of the center. Here are graphs showing the horizontal and vertical distances…",
