    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L10-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Back to Where We Started",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Is it possible to have a rotation that no matter how many times it repeats, you never end up back exactly at \\(P\\)? Explain your reasoning.",
