    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U06-L10-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "10.3: Back to Where We Started",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Notice that when the angle measure increases by \\(2\\pi\\), the \\(x\\)-coordinate of point \\(P\\) stays the same. This makes sense because \\(2\\pi\\) radians is a full rotation. In terms of functions, the cosine function, \\(\\cos(\\theta)\\), gives…",
